---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SectionBand from '@components/SectionBand.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '@components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import Button from '@components/Button.astro';
import AlumniGallery from '@components/AlumniGallery.astro';
import { practice } from '@data/site';
import { alumni } from '@data/alumni';

const title = 'Medical Assistant Careers in Dana Point';
const description =
  'We hire pre-PA and pre-med medical assistants and train them at the exam table. Two of our physician assistants started in that role. How the path works, and how to apply.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path="/join-us/">
  <!-- 1 · Hero -->
  <SectionBand as="div" class="hero">
    <Breadcrumbs
      crumbs={[
        { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
        { label: 'Join us', href: '/join-us/' },
      ]}
    />
    <div class="hero__copy" data-reveal>
      <span class="eyebrow">Join us</span>
      <h1>Two of our physician assistants started here as medical assistants.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        For about twenty years, this practice has hired college graduates on their way to PA or
        medical school, trained them at the exam table, and sent them off to their programs. More
        than 100 people have come through that way. We’re hiring the next medical assistant now.
      </p>
      <div class="hero__cta">
        <Button href="#apply" variant="primary">How to apply</Button>
        <Button href="#the-path" variant="secondary">How the path works ↓</Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </SectionBand>

  <!-- 2 · How the path works -->
  <SectionBand id="the-path" tone="evergreen" aria-labelledby="path-heading">
    <div class="band-prose" data-reveal>
      <h2 id="path-heading">How the path works</h2>
      <p>
        The role is medical assistant. It’s a real clinical job — rooming patients, preparing rooms
        and instruments, assisting during procedures, and keeping a busy dermatology practice
        moving.
      </p>
      <p>
        The training isn’t a classroom program. You work next to Dr. Moinfar and the physician
        assistants, and you learn the way they did: seeing the conditions in person, hearing how a
        diagnosis gets made, doing the parts you’re cleared to do and watching the rest.
      </p>
      <p>
        Over about twenty years, more than 100 pre-PA and pre-med graduates have worked here on
        their way to a program. A number of them are now physician assistants or physicians.
        Madeline Fee and Shylie Falahati, two of the physician assistants on staff now, both started
        here as medical assistants, went to PA school, and came back.
      </p>
    </div>
  </SectionBand>

  <!-- 3 · What the job actually is -->
  <SectionBand aria-labelledby="job-heading">
    <div class="prose" data-reveal>
      <h2 id="job-heading">What the job actually is</h2>
      <p>
        A medical assistant here rooms patients and records their history, sets up and assists with
        biopsies and excisions, works alongside Dr. Lander on Mohs surgery days, assists with
        cosmetic procedures, handles patient callbacks, and documents visits in the practice’s
        record system. The room turns over quickly and the day is full.
      </p>
      <p>
        You’re given real responsibility early, which also means the first few months are a lot to
        absorb. It’s a demanding job, and most people do it for a year or two before moving on to a
        program. That’s the design, not a failure of it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </SectionBand>

  <!-- 4 · Why people leave, addressed directly -->
  <SectionBand tone="fog" aria-labelledby="leave-heading">
    <div class="prose" data-reveal>
      <h2 id="leave-heading">People leave this job. That’s the point.</h2>
      <p>
        Most people who take this role are using it as a deliberate step toward PA school, medical
        school, or nursing, and we hire knowing that. When someone is ready to apply, they leave
        with clinical hours that hold up, a reference from a board-certified dermatologist who
        trained them, and help thinking through where to apply.
      </p>
      <p>
        Dermatology has a turnover problem. Here, people leave for a reason we’re glad to have been
        part of.
      </p>
    </div>
  </SectionBand>

  <!-- 5 · Where they are now -->
  <SectionBand aria-labelledby="now-heading">
    <p class="now__intro" data-reveal>
      As alumni give us permission to include them, this is where the last twenty years have gone.
      Names and photos are added only with a signed release.
    </p>
    <AlumniGallery heading="Where they are now" entries={alumni} />
  </SectionBand>

  <!-- 6 · Who this is for -->
  <SectionBand tone="fog" aria-labelledby="fit-heading">
    <div class="prose" data-reveal>
      <h2 id="fit-heading">Who this is for</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>A good fit</strong> if you have a science background and a specific plan — PA school,
        medical school, or nursing — and you want clinical hours that will stand up in an application.
        If you’re reliable, quick to learn, and comfortable being told when something is wrong.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Not the right fit</strong> if you’re looking for a long-term administrative role, if you
        need a predictable pace and a fixed schedule, or if you’re not planning to go on to a clinical
        program. None of that is a criticism — it’s just not what this particular job is.
      </p>
    </div>
  </SectionBand>

  <!-- 7 · How to apply -->
  <SectionBand id="apply" aria-labelledby="apply-heading">
    <div class="prose" data-reveal>
      <h2 id="apply-heading">How to apply</h2>
      <p>
        Email a resume and a short note — why now, and what you’re aiming for — to
        <a
          class="link-underline"
          href="mailto:derm@dermsc.com?subject=Medical%20assistant%20application">derm@dermsc.com</a
        >
        with “Medical assistant” in the subject line. If you’d rather call, the practice number is
        <a class="link-underline" href={`tel:${practice.phoneHref}`}>{practice.phone}</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        We read every application that comes in. If it looks like a fit, you’ll come in to meet the
        team and spend time in the clinic before anyone decides.
      </p>
    </div>
  </SectionBand>

  <!-- 8 · Closing CTA -->
  <SectionBand tone="evergreen-deep" aria-labelledby="cta-heading">
    <div class="closing" data-reveal>
      <h2 id="cta-heading">Apply</h2>
      <p>
        Send a resume and a short note about where you’re headed. If it’s a fit, we’ll bring you in
        to meet the team and see the clinic.
      </p>
      <div class="closing__cta">
        <Button
          href="mailto:derm@dermsc.com?subject=Medical%20assistant%20application"
          variant="primary"
        >
          Email your resume
        </Button>
        <Button href={`tel:${practice.phoneHref}`} variant="secondary">
          Call {practice.phone}
        </Button>
      </div>
      <p class="closing__cross">
        Want to know how the practice is set up first?
        <a class="link-underline" href="/about/">About Advanced Dermatology</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </SectionBand>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .section-title {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
  }

  /* Hero */
  .hero {
    padding-block: var(--space-12) var(--section-y);
  }
  .hero__copy {
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
  }
  .hero .lede {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    max-width: 60ch;
  }
  .hero__cta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
  }

  /* Generic prose */
  .prose {
    max-width: 60ch;
  }
  .prose h2 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }
  .prose p + p {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }

  /* Evergreen band prose */
  .band-prose {
    max-width: 60ch;
  }
  .band-prose h2 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }
  .band-prose p + p {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
  }

  /* Where they are now */
  .now__intro {
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    color: var(--stone);
  }

  /* Closing */
  .closing {
    max-width: 60ch;
  }
  .closing h2 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }
  .closing__cta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
  }
  .closing__cross {
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
    color: var(--stone);
  }
  /* Secondary "Call" button sits on the evergreen-deep band — lift it off the dark. */
  .closing__cta :global(.btn--secondary) {
    color: var(--paper);
    border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.4);
  }
  .closing__cta :global(.btn--secondary:hover) {
    color: var(--paper);
    border-color: var(--paper);
  }
</style>
